      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "So far it has been a pleasurable experience. Even on heavily overcast days we are producing electricity. On slightly overcast days we get around 5W and have seen peaks at 5.3W, strangely on bright blue days we average 4.5W for the peak times 11-1.30pm. It is quite a thrill seeing the old meter going backwards at around the same rate that it used to spin forwards. Now that Energex* has installed the new meter we will be able to see the actual data as the meters are digital.I have talked with neighbors who have systems and it seems that our Hyundai panels are out-performing other brands. I'm told that it may be due to the size of the cells. But on a per panel basis we are well ahead.Interestingly having the system has made the family energy conscious. (Somewhat counter intuitive but even our energy profligate users are switching off lights etc.)*One blip was the wait for Energex to connect the new meter but they came today and they were efficient, polite and nice.I will wait for a few months and then probably install another much larger system on a second property. Probably a 30KW system and if that goes well another.",
